  "question": {
    "text": "A line makes angles of $45^{\\circ}$ and $60^{\\circ}$ with the positive axes of $X$ and $Y$ respectively. The angle made by the same line with the positive axis of $Z$, is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$30^{\\circ}$ or $60^{\\circ}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$60^{\\circ}$ or $90^{\\circ}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$90^{\\circ}$ or $120^{\\circ}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$60^{\\circ}$ or $120^{\\circ}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $\\alpha=45^{\\circ}, \\beta=60^{\\circ}, \\gamma=?$\r\n\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\because \\cos ^{2} \\alpha+\\cos ^{2} \\beta+\\cos ^{2} \\gamma=1 \\\\\r\n\r\n\\therefore \\cos ^{2} \\gamma=1-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{y}=60^{\\circ} \\text { or } 120^{\\circ}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}$"
  }
}